        "summary": "A modified Boeing B-47 Stratojet flew for 80 hours, 36 minutes in 1959, setting an aviation record.",
        "body": [
          "A modified Boeing B-47 Stratojet took off from Wright-Patterson Air Force Base in Ohio at 03:13 local time on 27 November 1959. It remained airborne for 80 hours and 36 minutes, setting an aviation record. The aircraft repeatedly flew circuits across different parts of the United States and returned to the Dayton, Ohio, area for aerial refuelling.",
